{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516087-anastagio-s-olde-time-lunar-carnival-and-midnight-circus","id":1516087,"title":"Anastagio's Olde Time Lunar Carnival And Midnight Circus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-25T03:52:56-07:00","id":1516087,"title":"Anastagio's Olde Time Lunar Carnival And Midnight Circus","content":"Good evening class!<br /> <br /> Tonight's topic will be an interesting one, I hope at least; the 1996 World of Darkness: Midnight Circus!<br /> <br /> Step right up folks! Don't be shy! Come closer!<br /> Now, lets have a little fun!<br /> <br /> From the dawn of human civilization to the very End Times, the Midnight Circus was there - and probably will stay even after the world ended<br /> Namrael the Enochite, one of the earliest vampires - believed to be a daughter of Caine himself sacrificed her life and blood in those ancient times to strengthen the the Cult of the ancient goddess Cara, an Incarna of masks and exchange magical defences to continue...<br /> Alas the cult's purity didn't last: the cthonic god Apophis, freshly-banished from his homeland in Egypt, made contact with the itinerant priesthood in the hope that they could be used to spread the chaos that he was so devoted to. Bargaining with Cara directly, he proposed to extend the longevity of her rites in exchange for sacrifices in his name. Tragically, the Incarna realized the nature of Apophis too late, for though she was capable of preventing his dark powers from impacting her followers, she could not keep his influence at bay for ever; slowly, the cult was corrupted from within by its own patron.<br /> <br /> To the general public, the Citcusis a legitimate group of entertainers: an old-fashioned circus complete with animal shows, clowns, magicians, freaks, sideshow games and rides, visitors rarely - if ever - notice anything amiss in any of the performances, and few suspect that the managers are interested in anything other than mundane profit. However, this is only because the Circus carefully disguises its true nature with a powerful Glamour Veil, preventing any of the audience members from observing the murder and mistreatment that occurs on a daily basis throughout the show.<br /> In reality, the Midnight Circus is an active force for corruption with the World Of Darkness, and exists solely to spread moral and spiritual pollution by any means available. Every single show, ride, sideshow game or service provided by the carnival has been specifically designed to corrupt human souls, if not simply remove them altogether: in its wake, the Circus leaves a trail of soulless or spiritually-defiled victims, many of whom are driven to criminal acts as a result of their corruption. Whether fragmentary or forfeit, the Circus claims the souls of its audience for its own sinister purposes, usually to harvest their spiritual power; however, the Circus must also pay off its Patrons, and at the end of every last night in town, the representatives of the &quot;Old Shareholders&quot; arrive to collect their cut of the profits.<br /> These shareholders are in fact Apophis and the Wyrm, two powerful evil entities within the World Of Darkness: primordial creatures of perversion and chaos, darkness and destruction, they have sponsored the Circus solely for its ability to spread corruption wherever it goes - and, of course, for its generosity in providing them with more souls to consume.<br /> <br /> As such, unlike other villainous organizations like the Sabbat, the Technocracy or Pentex, the Midnight Circus has no grand plan in mind: its only goal is to remain active and continue corrupting the world at large.<br /> <br /> Possibly the most ambitious crossover <i>ever </i>one of the Midnight Circus' greatest strengths lies in its diversity: populated by vampires, mages, shapeshifters, fairies, ghosts and the possessed, the sheer range of powers on offer ensures that homogeneous groups cannot stop them.<br /> <br /> Old and a bit dusty book, and after almost three decades needs a bit tweeking, but still one of the most interesting supplement in my humble opinion to the World of Darkness<br /> <br /> My question is simple:<br /> <br /> How many of you used (or will use) the Circus in your stories? <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T04:25:56-07:00","id":1516089,"title":"","content":"I ran it ages ago, I never felt like taking another look at it.<br /> <br /> Conceptually the circus's independence causes a coherence issue in that there's no reason for more powerful forces in the (like say the Technocracy) not to wipe it out. Even if it implied some level of straining their resources, most of heir primary enemies (aka the Traditions) are going to be perfectly happy to take a break from Ascension warring and let the HITMarks go nuts on something else; assuming they don't help from the sidelines. Meanwhile your average PCs are going to, well, lose. Horribly. The diversity is a big problem because there's always something that can hit where the PCs are weak, and plenty of the circus's NPCs aren't push overs.<br /> <br /> Basically, the most likely outcomes are either (a) the PCs try to handle it, and they're going to die or worse, which could be fun if everyone wants that but that's not normally the case IME, or (b) the PCs realize they need to call in the big guns and then duck for cover while some heavy hitter in the setting deals with it. Outside of a supposed-to-be high body count one-shot, there's not a lot of appeal to that.<br /> <br /> It would be a lot more interesting if the circus was less &quot;clownishly evil with the power to back it up,&quot; and more ambiguous. More subtle and more clever core characters that let the circus go under the radar more convincingly would go a long way to make it more of a classic instead of a crazy diversion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T00:33:33-07:00","id":1516948,"title":"","content":"\u2018Something Wicked This Way Comes\u2019 is one of my all time favourite books, however agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> singularly the WOD Carnival is too big a problem for one of the factions not to erase it but too powerful to for a group.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the writers nod to the book, but I think it would have been more interesting as a neutral faction of assembled ancients who are using their combined powers to stay outside of the various conflicts and travel to maintain the enchantment, honour old pacts and accumulate quintessential power.<br /> <br /> From the triatic forces perspective it serves a purpose which they strangely all respect but what the purpose is, is a mystery.<br /> <br /> This could have provided a backdrop where the carnival is still dangerous \u201cEnter at your own peril\u201d or \u201cYou may go anywhere in the castle but those bedrooms\u201d but would see a mix of truly good, indifferent and truly evil all travelling together through their shared desire to remain outside.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d have it that some of their waypoints are significant in maintaining old rituals or oaths with various significant triatic forces (and others) to maintain their neutrality, that way the carnival could also be a place where the PCs go to bargain for something rare in return for a favour or service.<br /> <br /> The price not quite Faustian but enough that they feel they leave with less than they entered.<br /> <br /> But it has to be discreet working through proxies and tends to only conduct such matters in small out of the way towns.<br /> <br /> It would be a place of strange wonder where mortals don\u2019t give up their souls but they do unwittingly trade a little of their essence to be dedazzled and enthralled, the mists, disbelief and delirium not fully working but leaving with something memorable that once gone people can\u2019t quite put their finger on it.<br /> <br /> Due to the protection it has and debts owed, its neutral ground for the Camarilla, Technocracy, Wyrm etc - \u201cHoly Ground highlander\u201d, <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T19:38:05-07:00","id":1517622,"title":"","content":"I worked a travelling show as a Argentine BBQ-chef. It's not as fun as it seems and I grew an intolerance of anyone on the streets, under the influence. It was twelve-hour work, six-days a week. In between set-ups, I had free-time, like a week off. With different States/countries and their Blue-laws, it was difficult to drink at times. Most of my coworkers slammed heroin in on their breaks and they drank and partied a lot, but, I drank by myself. They'd steal anything they could and I had to keep my chef-knife on me at all times (Rambo-knife: good for cutting meat). My guess is the supernatural got tired of me so I left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}